@startuml system-workflow
title Secure Vibe Delivery — Workflow (a go-live check of one project)

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam ArrowColor #444444
skinparam ArrowFontColor #333333
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF7E0
skinparam NoteBorderColor #E0C46C

actor "Developer" as User #ECEFF1
participant "AI Assistant" as AST #E3F2FD
participant "MCP Server" as MCP #E8F5E9
participant "Doctor" as DOC #FFF3E0
participant "Run Pipeline" as PIPE #FFF3E0
participant "Security\nCheck" as SEC #F3E5F5
participant "Functional\nCheck" as FUN #F3E5F5
participant "Performance\nCheck" as PERF #F3E5F5
participant "Local\nToolchain" as TOOLS #E3F2FD
boundary "Snyk · Semgrep\n· PyPI/npm" as CLOUD #ECEFF1
boundary "Test\nenvironment" as TEST #ECEFF1
participant "Go-Live\nGate" as GATE #E8F5E9
participant "Report\nRenderer" as REND #E8F5E9
database "Run Records" as RUNS #ECEFF1

User -> AST : "check this project before go-live"

== Step 1 — Ask, check readiness, start the run ==
AST -> MCP : svd_doctor
MCP -> DOC : check tools
DOC -> TOOLS : versions · sign-ins
TOOLS --> DOC : all signed in
DOC --> AST : ready
AST -> MCP : svd_run
MCP -> PIPE : start background job
MCP --> AST : **run_id** (at once)

== Step 2 — Scan for security problems ==
activate PIPE
PIPE -> PIPE : detect project type
PIPE -> SEC : run
activate SEC
SEC -> TOOLS : snyk test / code / secrets · semgrep
TOOLS -> CLOUD : HTTPS (Snyk token)
CLOUD --> TOOLS : findings · rules
TOOLS --> SEC : JSON results
SEC -> CLOUD : package age (provenance)
SEC --> PIPE : **security result**
deactivate SEC

== Step 3 — Prove it works and copes with load ==
PIPE -> FUN : run
FUN -> TOOLS : pytest / Jest + coverage
TOOLS --> FUN : tests · coverage
FUN --> PIPE : **functional result**
PIPE -> PERF : run
PERF -> TOOLS : Locust at 1.5× peak
TOOLS -> TEST : load traffic
TEST --> TOOLS : responses
TOOLS --> PERF : p95 · errors
PERF --> PIPE : **performance result**
AST -> MCP : svd_status (polling)
MCP --> AST : progress

== Step 4 — Decide and report ==
PIPE -> GATE : three results
GATE --> PIPE : **verdict** + **must-fix list**
PIPE -> REND : render
REND -> RUNS : **HTML report** · PDF · summary.json
deactivate PIPE
PIPE --> User : opens **HTML report**
AST -> MCP : svd_report · svd_skill
MCP --> AST : verdict · must-fix · fixing guide
AST --> User : 📄 verdict and what to fix first

note across
  The server never calls Snyk's API itself: the Security Check starts the
  Snyk CLI as a local subprocess, and the CLI calls Snyk cloud with the token
  from a browser sign-in. The run is a background job, so the assistant
  polls svd_status instead of waiting on one long tool call.
end note

@enduml
